Scope
-----

The licence covers the *derived datasets* (the normalised JSON in `data/`): the
selection, normalisation, de-duplication, part-of-speech tagging and
provenance metadata added by this project. It does not transfer any rights in
the upstream files themselves, which remain the property of their respective
copyright holders and are never redistributed by this project. The corpus index
in `data/corpus.json` publishes metadata only.

The original fictional reading materials in src/data/reading-content.ts are
AI-assisted original writing released under CC BY 4.0 to the extent the project
holds rights. No passages, prompts, answers, audio or code from
ngoclong1209/UPGRADE-YOUR-IELTS-SKILLS are redistributed. That repository informed
a structural review only; its publicly visible files do not establish an open
licence. See docs/UPSTREAM-REVIEW.md for the pinned review and limitations.

The band descriptors in `src/data/bands.ts` are original condensed paraphrases
written for this project. They are not the official IELTS band descriptors,
which are published by the British Council, IDP: IELTS Australia and Cambridge
Assessment English (https://www.ielts.org/for-organisations/ielts-scoring-in-detail).
Researchers who need the authoritative wording must cite the published
descriptors directly.

The score concordances in `src/data/conversions.ts` are indicative values
compiled from the test providers' own published comparison tables. Receiving
institutions apply their own rules; always verify against the current published
table.

